dence interval of 5.3 to 17.5. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 10% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,037.93 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove misconduct. Prices might be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't show wrongdoing without more context.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts are unusually frequent. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same need. Look at contract [1] to see what was bought and if it matches other similar contracts.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["qaKSvSrqhXVVq4S9zvaQpQ%3D%3D","XImr5PDhmRO7JOCXkOhcDg%3D%3D","WqjQ0XrZiIVVq4S9zvaQpQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}